[27.814448, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# 6. Every application is tracked with its fit prediction. Closing a season audits you:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[29.819571, "o", "\u001b[1m$ mkdir -p /var/folders/pk/c_260r6n23d41183qgb_7tvh0000gn/T/tmp.E9Bsb1Bs27/home && cp -r examples/sam-rivera/searches /var/folders/pk/c_260r6n23d41183qgb_7tvh0000gn/T/tmp.E9Bsb1Bs27/home/ && cd /var/folders/pk/c_260r6n23d41183qgb_7tvh0000gn/T/tmp.E9Bsb1Bs27/home && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\n# reopen the example season so the demo can close it live\r\nimport pathlib, re\r\np = pathlib.Path('searches/2026/applications.md')\r\np.write_text(re.sub(r'^Status: CLOSED [0-9-]+\\.', 'Status: OPEN.', p.read_text(), flags=re.M))\r\npathlib.Path('searches/2026/retro.md').unlink()\r\nEOF\r\npython3 \"/Users/case/Documents/GitHub/career-template\"/engine/season.py close 2026 && head -13 searches/2026/retro.md && cd \"/Users/case/Documents/GitHub/career-template\" >/dev/null\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[30.597834, "o", "closed season 2026: wrote searches/2026/retro.md, stamped tracker\r\n"]
[30.603388, "o", "# Season 2026 retro\r\n\r\nClosed 2026-09-11. Calibration: predicted fit vs what happened.\r\n\r\n| Company | Role | Predicted fit | Final stage | Days to first response |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Linear | Senior/Staff Product Engineer, AI | 75% | rejected | 9 |\r\n| Cognition | Product Engineer | 65% | ghosted | — |\r\n| Vanta | Senior SWE, AI Product | 80% | offer | 4 |\r\n| Mintlify | Senior Product Engineer | 70% | withdrawn | 6 |\r\n| Temporal | Staff SWE, AI Foundations | 60% | rejected | 13 |\r\n\r\n## Reads\r\n"]
[33.610473, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# The retro is the product: predicted fit vs what actually happened,\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.819329, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2m# so the NEXT search starts from evidence, not vibes.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[36.828049, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32mIt prepares. \u001b[1mYou review, you submit.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
